/-!
# Orbits over a sufficiently large algebraically closed field

Let `j : R ⟶ U ×_B U` be a pre-relation of algebraic spaces over an algebraic space `B`, and
let `p` be a geometric point of `B` with algebraically closed field `k`. Two points of `U`
over `p` are equivalent when a chain of arrows of `j` joins them over some extension of `k`,
and weakly equivalent when such a chain exists over `k` itself. The two notions agree as soon
as `k` is larger than every residue field of a scheme atlas of the relation generated by `j`:
a chain over an extension field is a single arrow of the generated relation, and an arrow of
an algebraic space lying over a `k`-valued point of `U ×_B U` is itself represented by a
`k`-valued point once `k` is that large.

## Main definitions

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.IsLargeField`: a field is larger than the invariant
  `λ F = sup {ℵ₀, |κ(u)| : u ∈ W}` of a presheaf `F`, computed on a scheme atlas `W → F`.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.rel_of_rel_after_extension_of_large_field`: over a large enough
  field, an arrow of a pre-relation which exists after an extension of the field exists
  already over the field itself.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.orbit_eq_weakOrbit_of_isPreEquivalenceRelation_of_large_field`:
  weak orbits and orbits of a pre-equivalence relation agree over a large enough field.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.orbit_eq_weakOrbit_of_large_field` and
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.equivalent_iff_weaklyEquivalent_of_large_field`: **Stacks 048U,
  part (2)** for an arbitrary pre-relation.

## Implementation notes

"Sufficiently large" is the condition `|k| > λ(R_∞)` of the source, where `R_∞` is the
relation generated by the pre-relation; this is the hypothesis under which a point of an
algebraic space lifts over `k`. It is stated through a scheme atlas of `R_∞`, which is how
`λ` is computed, and the atlas is existentially quantified so that the hypothesis is the
weakest of the equivalent ones. The bound has to be measured against the relation: every
field whose spectrum is an object of the site has cardinality below the size cutoff of the
site, so a bound formulated by that cutoff is met by no geometric point at all.

Weak orbits and orbits are those of a pre-relation of presheaves over the presheaf of `B`,
while the relation generated by a pre-relation lives in the slice of the algebraic spaces
over `B`; the two are joined by `AlgebraicGeometry.Space.presheafPreRelation`, exactly as
for the orbits of the generated relation.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 048U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/048U)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits

universe u

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Space

/-- A field `k` is *large* for a presheaf `F` on the big fppf site over `S` when some
surjective étale atlas `W → F` by an object of the site has all its residue fields of
cardinality smaller than `k`, and `k` is uncountable; that is, when `|k| > λ F` for the
invariant `λ F = sup {ℵ₀, |κ(u)| : u ∈ W}`.

The invariant does not depend on the atlas, so the existential quantifier could equally be
universal; it is the shape in which the condition is used to lift a point of `F` over `k`. -/
def IsLargeField (site : BigFppfSite.{u}) (S : Scheme.{u}) (hS : site.Contains S)
    (F : (BigFppfOver site S hS)ᵒᵖ ⥤ Type u) (k : Type u) [Field k] : Prop :=
  ∃ (W : BigFppfOver site S hS) (w : yoneda.obj W ⟶ F),
    (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Surjective.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme site S hS))) w ∧
    (MorphismProperty.presheaf (MorphismProperty.inverseImage
      (@Etale.{u} : MorphismProperty Scheme.{u})
      (BigFppfOver.toScheme site S hS))) w ∧
    Cardinal.aleph0 ⊔ ⨆ u : (BigFppfOver.toScheme site S hS).obj W,
        Cardinal.mk (((BigFppfOver.toScheme site S hS).obj W).residueField u) <
      Cardinal.mk k

variable {site : BigFppfSite.{u}} {S : Scheme.{u}} {hS : site.Contains S}
  {B : AlgebraicSpaces site S hS} {R U : Over B}

/-- Over a sufficiently large algebraically closed field, an arrow of a pre-relation joining
two points of `U` after an extension of the field already joins them over the field itself.

The pair of points is a point of `U ×_B U` over the field, and the arrow over the extension
exhibits a point of `R` above it; the point of `R` is then represented over the field itself
because the field is larger than the residue fields of an atlas of `R`. -/
theorem rel_of_rel_after_extension_of_large_field (j : PreRelation R U)
    (p : GeometricPoint site S hS B.obj)
    (hp : IsLargeField site S hS R.left.obj p.val.carrier)
    {x y : TestPoint p.val.siteObject (yonedaEquiv.symm p.val.value)
      ((overForgetSpace B).obj U)}
    {q : FieldValuedPoint site S hS B.obj} (f : q.siteObject ⟶ p.val.siteObject)
    (hf : B.obj.map f.op p.val.value = q.value)
    {x' y' : TestPoint q.siteObject (yonedaEquiv.symm q.value) ((overForgetSpace B).obj U)}
    (hx : x'.1 = yoneda.map f ≫ x.1) (hy : y'.1 = yoneda.map f ≫ y.1)
    (h : (presheafPreRelation j).Rel (yonedaEquiv.symm q.value) y' x') :
    (presheafPreRelation j).Rel (yonedaEquiv.symm p.val.value) y x := by
  classical
  obtain ⟨W, w, hwSurj, hwEtale, hcard⟩ := hp
  obtain ⟨r, hrt, hrs⟩ := (rel_presheafPreRelation_iff j y' x').mp h
  -- The two points, read as one point of `U ×_B U`, over the field and over its extension.
  let pair : representableOver (B := B) p.val.siteObject (yonedaEquiv.symm p.val.value) ⟶
      U ⨯ U := prod.lift (testPointOver y) (testPointOver x)
  -- The extension of fields, read as a morphism of representable algebraic spaces.
  have hfb : yoneda.map f ≫ yonedaEquiv.symm p.val.value = yonedaEquiv.symm q.value := by
    rw [yonedaEquiv_symm_naturality_left, hf]
  let fOver : representableOver (B := B) q.siteObject (yonedaEquiv.symm q.value) ⟶
      representableOver (B := B) p.val.siteObject (yonedaEquiv.symm p.val.value) :=
    testPointOver ⟨yoneda.map f, hfb⟩
  have hpairFst : pair ≫ prod.fst = testPointOver y := prod.lift_fst _ _
  have hpairSnd : pair ≫ prod.snd = testPointOver x := prod.lift_snd _ _
  have hpairq : r ≫ j = fOver ≫ pair := by
    refine prod.hom_ext ?_ ?_
    · simp only [Category.assoc, hpairFst]
      refine Over.OverMorphism.ext (ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ ?_)
      change (r ≫ j.target).left.hom = yoneda.map f ≫ y.1
      rw [← hy, ← hrt]
      rfl
    · simp only [Category.assoc, hpairSnd]
      refine Over.OverMorphism.ext (ObjectProperty.hom_ext _ ?_)
      change (r ≫ j.source).left.hom = yoneda.map f ≫ x.1
      rw [← hx, ← hrs]
      rfl
  -- The point of `R` over the extension, and the point of `U ×_B U` over the field.
  let rNat : yoneda.obj q.siteObject ⟶ R.left.obj := r.left.hom
  let pairNat : yoneda.obj p.val.siteObject ⟶ (U ⨯ U : Over B).left.obj := pair.left.hom
  have hrj : rNat ≫ j.left.hom = yoneda.map f ≫ pairNat :=
    congrArg (fun g : representableOver (B := B) q.siteObject (yonedaEquiv.symm q.value) ⟶
      U ⨯ U ↦ g.left.hom) hpairq
  have hdom : (U ⨯ U : Over B).left.obj.map f.op (yonedaEquiv pairNat) =
      j.left.hom.app (Opposite.op q.siteObject) (yonedaEquiv rNat) := by
    rw [yonedaEquiv_naturality, ← yonedaEquiv_comp, hrj]
  have hxy : pointsMap site S hS R.left.obj j.left.hom
        ((⟨q.carrier, q.contained, q.toBase, yonedaEquiv rNat⟩ :
          FieldValuedPoint site S hS R.left.obj).class site S hS R.left.obj) =
      (⟨p.val.carrier, p.val.contained, p.val.toBase, yonedaEquiv pairNat⟩ :
        FieldValuedPoint site S hS (U ⨯ U : Over B).left.obj).class site S hS
          (U ⨯ U : Over B).left.obj :=
    FieldValuedPoint.class_eq_class_of_hasCommonExtension site S hS _
      ⟨_, FieldValuedPoint.dominates_refl site S hS _ _, ⟨f, hdom⟩⟩
  -- The point of `R` is represented over the field itself.
  have : IsAlgClosed p.val.carrier := p.property
  obtain ⟨z, hz, -⟩ := exists_lift_of_large_field site S hS R.left.property
    (U ⨯ U : Over B).left.property j.left.hom W w hwSurj hwEtale p.val.carrier
    p.val.contained p.val.toBase hcard
    ((⟨q.carrier, q.contained, q.toBase, yonedaEquiv rNat⟩ :
      FieldValuedPoint site S hS R.left.obj).class site S hS R.left.obj)
    (yonedaEquiv pairNat) hxy
  have hzj : yonedaEquiv.symm z ≫ j.left.hom = pair.left.hom := by
    rw [yonedaEquiv_symm_naturality_right, hz]
    exact yonedaEquiv.symm_apply_apply _
  have hzb : yonedaEquiv.symm z ≫ R.hom.hom = yonedaEquiv.symm p.val.value := by
    rw [← over_w_hom j, ← Category.assoc, hzj]
    exact over_w_hom pair
  refine (rel_presheafPreRelation_iff j y x).mpr
    ⟨testPointOver ⟨yonedaEquiv.symm z, hzb⟩, Subtype.ext ?_, Subtype.ext ?_⟩
  · change yonedaEquiv.symm z ≫ j.target.left.hom = y.1
    rw [show j.target.left.hom = j.left.hom ≫ (prod.fst : U ⨯ U ⟶ U).left.hom from rfl,
      ← Category.assoc, hzj]
    exact congrArg (fun g : _ ⟶ U ↦ g.left.hom) hpairFst
  · change yonedaEquiv.symm z ≫ j.source.left.hom = x.1
    rw [show j.source.left.hom = j.left.hom ≫ (prod.snd : U ⨯ U ⟶ U).left.hom from rfl,
      ← Category.assoc, hzj]
    exact congrArg (fun g : _ ⟶ U ↦ g.left.hom) hpairSnd

/-- Over a sufficiently large algebraically closed field, the weak orbit of a point of `U`
under a pre-equivalence relation is its orbit: for such a relation both are cut out by a
single arrow, and an arrow available after an extension of the field is already available
over the field. -/
theorem orbit_eq_weakOrbit_of_isPreEquivalenceRelation_of_large_field (j : PreRelation R U)
    (hj : IsPreEquivalenceRelation (presheafPreRelation j))
    (p : GeometricPoint site S hS B.obj)
    (hp : IsLargeField site S hS R.left.obj p.val.carrier)
    (x : TestPoint p.val.siteObject (yonedaEquiv.symm p.val.value)
      ((overForgetSpace B).obj U)) :
    (presheafPreRelation j).orbit p x = (presheafPreRelation j).weakOrbit p x := by
  rw [PreRelation.orbit_eq_targets_after_extension _ hj p x,
    PreRelation.weakOrbit_eq_targets _ hj p x]
  ext y
  constructor
  · rintro ⟨q, f, hf, x', y', hx, hy, hrel⟩
    exact rel_of_rel_after_extension_of_large_field j p hp f hf hx hy hrel
  · intro hyx
    exact ⟨p.val, 𝟙 _, by simp, x, y, by simp, by simp, hyx⟩

/-- **Stacks 048U, part (2).** Over a sufficiently large algebraically closed field the orbit
of a point of `U` under a pre-relation is its weak orbit over the same field: no extension of
the field is needed. The bound is on the relation generated by the pre-relation, and is
uniform in the geometric point and in the point whose orbit is taken. -/
@[stacks 048U "large_field_orbits"]
theorem orbit_eq_weakOrbit_of_large_field {j : PreRelation R U} (P : PathConstruction j)
    (p : GeometricPoint site S hS B.obj)
    (hp : IsLargeField site S hS P.allPaths.left.obj p.val.carrier)
    (x : TestPoint p.val.siteObject (yonedaEquiv.symm p.val.value)
      ((overForgetSpace B).obj U)) :
    (presheafPreRelation j).orbit p x = (presheafPreRelation j).weakOrbit p x := by
  rw [← orbit_allPathsRelation P p x, ← weakOrbit_allPathsRelation P p x]
  exact orbit_eq_weakOrbit_of_isPreEquivalenceRelation_of_large_field P.allPathsRelation
    (isPreEquivalenceRelation_allPathsRelation P) p hp x

/-- **Stacks 048U, part (2).** Over a sufficiently large algebraically closed field,
equivalence of two points of `U` under a pre-relation is their weak equivalence over the same
field. The bound is on the relation generated by the pre-relation, and is uniform in the
geometric point and in the pair of points. -/
@[stacks 048U "large_field_equivalence"]
theorem equivalent_iff_weaklyEquivalent_of_large_field {j : PreRelation R U}
    (P : PathConstruction j) (p : GeometricPoint site S hS B.obj)
    (hp : IsLargeField site S hS P.allPaths.left.obj p.val.carrier)
    (x y : TestPoint p.val.siteObject (yonedaEquiv.symm p.val.value)
      ((overForgetSpace B).obj U)) :
    (presheafPreRelation j).Equivalent p.val x y ↔
      (presheafPreRelation j).WeaklyEquivalent p.val x y :=
  Iff.of_eq (congrArg (y ∈ ·) (orbit_eq_weakOrbit_of_large_field P p hp x))

end AlgebraicGeometry.Space

end
